;; Boundary keep-set regression (docs/index-reuse.md).  r is built early,
;; IGNORED by the middle stratum -- whose boundary must keep r's trees
;; without dumping them (the unread-relation arm of the sweep) -- and read
;; again by a late stratum, which must see ALL of r through its own
;; boundary's marked dump.  The ground (out 1 2), duplicating a derived
;; row, pins the ordinary-batch intern against a kept master: it must null
;; against the surviving content exactly as it would have against a
;; rebuilt one (out stays 6 rows).
table (edge int int)
table (r int int)
table (a int)
table (b int)
table (out int int)

rule (edge 1 2) (edge 2 3) (edge 3 4)

rule (edge X Y) --> (r X Y)
rule (r X Y) (edge Y Z) --> (r X Z)

rule (a 10) (a 11)
rule (a X) --> (b X)

rule (out 1 2)
rule (r X Y) (b A) (= A 10) --> (out X Y)
